45417] [17592186542191 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "afcfe65d-5017-5ca6-9a0c-f6939bdd2a4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542191 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-5I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-5I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186551364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186551391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186551416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186551422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186551460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550355 #edb/ref 1045 "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Where